WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.212
At the sound of the maid's scream, Kathleen ran into Gerald's room.

2
00:00:07.213 --> 00:00:08.985
"What's wrong?"

3
00:00:08.986 --> 00:00:12.901
"One minute Gerald was gone!" said Eliza.

4
00:00:12.902 --> 00:00:15.668
"The next minute he was in the bed!

5
00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:17.954
I don't know what's wrong with me.

6
00:00:17.955 --> 00:00:22.337
Yesterday I was hearing voices, and now this."

7
00:00:22.338 --> 00:00:28.830
Eliza shook her head as she left the room.

8
00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:33.205
"What happened?" Kathleen asked Gerald.

9
00:00:33.206 --> 00:00:36.237
"The ring came off when Eliza called me.

10
00:00:36.238 --> 00:00:41.634
I'm hungry. I'll tell you everything later."

11
00:00:41.635 --> 00:00:47.248
After breakfast Gerald remembered he'd left the ring in bed.

12
00:00:47.249 --> 00:00:52.594
But when he went upstairs, Eliza had already made his bed.

13
00:00:52.595 --> 00:00:55.716
He asked her about the ring.

14
00:00:55.717 --> 00:00:58.688
"I didn't see anything," she said.

15
00:00:58.689 --> 00:01:04.411
"If there was a ring in the bed, I'd have seen it."

16
00:01:04.412 --> 00:01:10.948
The children searched every corner of the room, but couldn't find the ring.

17
00:01:10.949 --> 00:01:17.418
Soon they gave up because they had to meet Mabel in town.

18
00:01:17.419 --> 00:01:20.290
They sat on a wall to wait for her.

19
00:01:20.291 --> 00:01:29.414
"Hey, you went back to normal faster than I did," Mabel said to Gerald.

20
00:01:29.415 --> 00:01:34.905
Now Gerald could tell the story of the three burglars.

21
00:01:34.906 --> 00:01:42.670
After throwing the rock, he'd returned to the room where they were loading their sacks.

22
00:01:42.671 --> 00:01:49.881
He'd followed the men out into the night and discovered their hiding place.

23
00:01:49.882 --> 00:01:53.727
"Look, there's Officer Johnson," said Gerald.

24
00:01:53.728 --> 00:01:58.120
"I need to talk to him."

25
00:01:58.121 --> 00:02:03.951
Gerald hopped off the wall and went over to Officer Johnson.

26
00:02:03.952 --> 00:02:09.387
"Would you like to catch those burglars who've been stealing silver?"

27
00:02:09.388 --> 00:02:13.253
"What do you know about that?" Johnson asked suspiciously.

28
00:02:13.254 --> 00:02:17.561
"I saw something last night, but I could get in trouble for being out late.

29
00:02:17.562 --> 00:02:19.632
Do you promise not to tell anyone?"

30
00:02:19.633 --> 00:02:21.871
Johnson nodded.

31
00:02:21.872 --> 00:02:24.779
"I saw three men taking silver from the castle.

32
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.751
I know where they put it."

33
00:02:26.752 --> 00:02:30.925
"So you wrote the note?" Johnson said eagerly.

34
00:02:30.926 --> 00:02:37.834
"Yes." Gerald explained how he'd watched the men go down to the river. They

35
00:02:37.835 --> 00:02:42.074
had tied their bags of silver under a dock. Tonight,

36
00:02:42.075 --> 00:02:47.619
after dark, they planned to retrieve the silver and escape by boat. "You

37
00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.074
can catch them then," said Gerald. "But

38
00:02:51.075 --> 00:02:55.851
which dock is their hiding spot?" asked Johnson. "Follow

39
00:02:55.852 --> 00:03:00.816
me," said Gerald. "When

40
00:03:00.817 --> 00:03:05.723
I take out my handkerchief and blow my nose, that'll be the place." Gerald

41
00:03:05.724 --> 00:03:10.130
went back to the other children. "Come

42
00:03:10.131 --> 00:03:15.193
on! Let's play follow-the-leader." The

43
00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:20.669
children followed him, running and jumping and imitating his every step. Johnson

44
00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:26.643
followed at a distance. On

45
00:03:26.644 --> 00:03:31.394
one dock Gerald suddenly stopped and blew his nose. Then

46
00:03:31.395 --> 00:03:41.040
he led the children back to the school. "We've

47
00:03:41.041 --> 00:03:43.983
brought our friend Mabel home for lunch," said

48
00:03:43.984 --> 00:03:47.089
Kathleen when Eliza opened the door. "Where's

49
00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.514
Mademoiselle?" "She's

50
00:03:49.515 --> 00:03:51.544
gone to visit the castle. The

51
00:03:51.545 --> 00:03:53.944
grounds are open to the public today. Now

52
00:03:53.945 --> 00:03:55.763
hurry up with your lunch. This

53
00:03:55.764 --> 00:03:57.723
is my afternoon off. My

54
00:03:57.724 --> 00:04:06.324
fiancé doesn't like waiting for me." The

55
00:04:06.325 --> 00:04:09.477
children ate quickly and Eliza left. "Where's

56
00:04:09.478 --> 00:04:13.024
the ring?" asked Mabel. "I

57
00:04:13.025 --> 00:04:15.590
really need to put it back." "I

58
00:04:15.591 --> 00:04:19.152
haven't had a turn yet," protested Jimmy. "When

59
00:04:19.153 --> 00:04:21.883
we find it—" "

60
00:04:21.884 --> 00:04:25.279
When you find it?" said Mabel.

61
00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.903
They told her about losing the ring.

62
00:04:29.904 --> 00:04:32.939
"Oh no!" cried Mabel.

63
00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:36.165
"We have to find it!"

64
00:04:36.166 --> 00:04:41.909
The children searched and searched Gerald's room, but they still couldn't find the ring.

65
00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:46.341
Suddenly there was pounding at the back door.

66
00:04:46.342 --> 00:04:48.722
Kathleen ran downstairs.

67
00:04:48.723 --> 00:04:53.818
A strange man stood near the doorstep.

68
00:04:53.819 --> 00:04:57.244
His eyes were open wide with amazement.

69
00:04:57.245 --> 00:05:00.215
One arm was stretched out toward the door.

70
00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:04.771
The rest of him looked as if he were trying to run the other way.

71
00:05:04.772 --> 00:05:07.570
"Let go of me!" he cried.

72
00:05:07.571 --> 00:05:11.562
"I won't let go of you!" said Eliza's voice.

73
00:05:11.563 --> 00:05:17.558
But no Eliza could be seen.

